  "TI_DN034_Yagi__2.4_GHz__directional"
  (at 100 100)
  (version 20221018)
  (generator pcb_antenna_designer)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Printed Yagi-Uda from TI design note DN034 (SWRA350), dimensions from its Figure 2: a dipole (L2) whose arms are on two copper layers 0.226 mm apart, three directors (L3-L5) and the ground plane as reflector, on a 150 x 100 mm, 1.6 mm 4-layer FR-4 board. TI measured about 7.2 dBi gain, a front-to-back ratio near 15 dB and a -10 dB band of 2126-2623 MHz. Parameter names as in the note. TI feeds it through a tapered balun that is not modelled here, so two values differ from the note: the dipole L2 is 40.5 mm (TI: 44.96) and the two-wire line WL is 0.4 mm (TI: 0.533). With them the feed is close to 50 ohm and the -10 dB band is about 2.32-2.61 GHz, which covers the 2.4 GHz band without a matching network. L2 moves the band, WL the impedance.")
  (tags "antenna IFA MIFA RF")
  (attr smd)
  (net_tie_pad_groups "1, 2")
